            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac thrombi mistaken for metastasis in recurrent melanoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S29-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2459/JCM.0b013e3283613967</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intra-cardiac thrombi can be incidentally found in recurrent melanoma and need careful assessment. An 81-year-old woman, with a history of malignant nasopharyngeal melanoma, was evaluated by echocardiography and cardiac magnetic resonance due to the detection of undefined masses localized both in right atrium and ventricle during contrast-enhanced thoraco-abdominal computed tomography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
